From 50587ac0cb174f0caaf7a52f977cb4aa8f4372db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Davidson Francis <davidsondfgl@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 2 Jun 2022 16:41:39 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Linenoise changes for Nanvix+Python

This patch is intended to replace the default Python fgets (for when
there is no libreadline) for Linenoise.

For this, a set of changes needed to be made so that the REPL
experience was not hampered.

Nanvix changes:
---------------
* Modifications required for Linenoise to work on Nanvix:
* Removal of terminal type identification
* Removal of column/row identification: always 80x25
* TCSAFLUSH -> TCSANOW in tcsetattr
* Disable linenoiseBeep()
* Change default enter key (13 -> 10)

Bug Fixes:
----------
Linenoise hates tab: whenever a tab is pressed the behavior becomes
quite erratic. This is because Linenoise assumes that the cursor
position is always a direct correspondent of the number of characters
in the buffer, which is not exactly true: a tab character ('\t') can
make the cursor skip several characters from just one time.

There are at least two solutions for this:
a) modify all Linenoise logic to account for tab characters.
b) convert all tabs to spaces.
Option b) is definitely the easiest and is the one implemented here.

Python changes:
---------------
In order to improve the Python experience: this patch also adds
support for syntax highlighting of lines of code, via libaqua.

Signed-off-by: Davidson Francis <davidsondfgl@gmail.com>
